  THE POPULATION THIS PART'S VERDICT IS ABOUT (rule 90, stated before the verdict):
    necklace hosts certified C4-free with mu >= 2 : 396
    ... IN CLASS (l > 4 AND rad >= 5)             : 393
    ... of those, CASE A hosts (diam = rad+1)     : 57
    On a CASE B host a condition-3 vertex at offset +1 is a counterexample to the
    restricted (RXM-PERI); on a CASE A host it is E44's object outright.  BOTH are
    findings, so no host in the table above is wasted -- but only the CASE A count
    measures the thing round 39's family could not reach.

  (CS-1') AS A DECISION PROCEDURE, APPLIED HOST BY HOST BEFORE ANY COUNTING.
  (CS-1') says a condition-3 vertex w has Ctr contained in the sphere S_rad(w),
  hence |Ctr| <= |S_rad(w)|.  So if |Ctr| > max_w |S_rad(w)| the host CANNOT carry
  a condition-3 vertex AT ALL -- proved, not measured.  Counting condition-3
  vertices on such a host is counting in a class that is provably empty.
    in-class CASE A hosts                                   : 57
    ... DECIDED EMPTY BY (CS-1') alone (|Ctr| > max_w |S_r(w)|): 53
    ... LIVE: condition 3 is not excluded by counting        : 4
      NLsd(6,s3)       n=120 rad=5 diam=6 l=4.650 |Ctr|= 25 max|S_r(w)|= 41
      NLkd(3^6,s3)     n=156 rad=5 diam=6 l=5.000 |Ctr|= 12 max|S_r(w)|= 44
